      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both ACE inhibitors (angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors) and ARBs (angiotensin receptor blockers) are top-tier, first-line choices for treating high blood pressure (hypertension) .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Both ACE inhibitors (angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors) and ARBs (angiotensin receptor blockers) are top-tier, first-line choices for treating high blood pressure (hypertension)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How They Work"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "ACE inhibitors (ending in -pril, like lisinopril) stop your body from producing angiotensin II, a hormone that narrows your blood vessels."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "ARBs (ending in -sartan, like losartan) let your body make angiotensin II, but they block the receptors so it cannot tighten your blood vessels."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Both relax blood vessels, lower blood pressure, and protect your heart and kidneys."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Differences as First-Line Choices"
